<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
  CompSapientMechReactiveArmor.cs doesn't exist on either ThingDef natively - it's an
  independent reimplementation of Mechanoids: Total Warfare's CompFuelBasedDamageReduction,
  not a patch on that mod's own comp - so it has to be added here first before
  HumanlikeAnimalSettings_MechQueens.xml's compWhitelist can let it survive into the
  sapient clone. The comp self-gates to sapient-only at runtime (see IsActive), so its
  presence on the non-sapient originals is harmless. Gated on Nyar.NCLvsTW (Mechanoids:
  Total Warfare) being installed - without it, this comp never gets added to either
  ThingDef in the first place, so the whitelist entry never has anything to let through.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Nyar.NCLvsTW">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mech_Warqueen"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechReactiveArmor" />
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Veltaris.Mechqueen,Nyar.NCLvsTW">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AV_Mech_Workerqueen"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechReactiveArmor" />
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!--
  Second, separate reactive-armor mechanic - an independent reimplementation of
  Glitterworld Destroyer 5's CompHitArmor/GD_HitArmor (see CompSapientMechHitArmor.cs
  and Hediffs_ReactiveArmor.xml): charge-limited full immunity for a short time after
  each hit, recharging via repair. Runs alongside CompProperties_SapientMechReactiveArmor
  above rather than replacing it, per explicit instruction - the two are independent
  comps with no shared state. Same duration (60 ticks) and charge count (15) GD5 uses
  for the War Queen; there's no equivalent source value for the Work Queen since GD5
  doesn't touch AV Framework at all, so the same numbers are reused there too. Gated on
  fxz.glitterworlddestroyer.mk5 (Glitterworld Destroyer 5) being installed, same
  reasoning as above.

  DISABLED IN FAVOR OF FIXING THE ORIGINAL (both Operations below, commented out) -
  GD3.CompProperties_HitArmor (GD5's own native comp) is separately whitelisted in
  HumanlikeAnimalSettings_MechQueens.xml and survives onto the sapient clone on its own,
  but its charges don't recharge via repair for a sapient mech even while a mechanitor
  is actively, successfully repairing it - confirmed by testing. Same "not built with
  sapient mechs in mind" gap every other GD5 comp in this mod needed its own fix for,
  not something specific to this mechanic. Rather than keep two independent comps doing
  the same thing (which is what caused the duplicate "Reactive Armor" gizmo this was
  investigating in the first place), this reimplementation stays disabled and the fix
  goes into GD3's own comp directly instead - see GD3_CompHitArmor_RepairRecharge_Patch.cs.
  -->

  <!--
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,fxz.glitterworlddestroyer.mk5">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mech_Warqueen"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechHitArmor">
        <hediffToAdd>SapientMechanoidFix_ReactiveArmor</hediffToAdd>
        <duration>60</duration>
        <limitOfTimes>15</limitOfTimes>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Veltaris.Mechqueen,fxz.glitterworlddestroyer.mk5">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AV_Mech_Workerqueen"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientMechHitArmor">
        <hediffToAdd>SapientMechanoidFix_ReactiveArmor</hediffToAdd>
        <duration>60</duration>
        <limitOfTimes>15</limitOfTimes>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  -->

</Patch>
